  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "Compute the variance ${\\sigma }^{2}$ of a data set ${x}_{i}$ consisting of $8$ data points, where\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i}=-112,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i}^{2}=1736.\n$$\n\n${\\sigma }^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},\u2026,{x}_{n},$ then the variance can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\overset{\u2015}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{\u2015}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{\u2015}{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overset{\u2015}{{x}^{2}}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{\u2015}{x}.$ There are $n=8$ points in our data set, and we know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i}=-112,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot (-112) \\\\  & =-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{\u2015}{{x}^{2}}.$ We know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i}^{2}=1736,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot 1736 \\\\  & =217.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{\u2015}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{\u2015}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =217-{(-14)}^{2} \\\\  & =217-196 \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
